{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1567424829,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0ODgxNDkzODQ=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3643","origin":"github"},"title":"`download-url` vs `addurls`?","message":"I would like to get feedback on the purpose of `download-url` now that we have `addurls`. There is a significant overlap. Additionally `download-url` needs an overhaul wrt path handling (e.g. use of `normpath` inside), i.e. transition it to use pathlib.\n\nQ is now: is there anything that speaks against stripping any functionality from `download-url` that works with datasets (e.g. actually saving downloaded files in a dataset)?\n\n#### Pros\n\n- it would make the command do what the name suggests -- download and download only\n- it would reduce the overlap with `addurls`\n\n#### Cons\n\n- it complicates adding a single/few files to a dataset from a set of URLs (but given there is `git annex addurl`, and `addurls` not much is lost)","files":null}]}